The address is drawn from the om network `network` names. On a lan network,
it is drawn the first time the resource starts and recorded in `addr`, which
every node then uses. The netmask is the one of the network, unless `netmask`
is set.

On a layer 2 network, as a l2_bridge one, om has no address to draw: the
interface joins the segment with no address and a stable hardware address,
for the container to ask one of a dhcp server of the segment.

Choose it to have om pick a free address of a network declared in the
cluster configuration, or to join a layer 2 segment.
